WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.467
-I love seeing you. Oh, my gosh.

00:00:02.467 --> 00:00:04.767
It's been three years,
almost to the day.

00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:05.901
-Almost to the day.

00:00:05.901 --> 00:00:07.133
-Yeah, and a lot of things
have happened.

00:00:07.133 --> 00:00:08.300
Congratulations.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.501
-What are you talking about?
-Oh, yeah.

00:00:09.501 --> 00:00:11.100
What am I talking about? Yeah.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:12.567
You have another baby
on the way.

00:00:12.567 --> 00:00:14.067
I do. I do.

00:00:14.067 --> 00:00:15.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:15.534 --> 00:00:18.300
-Hi, baby!

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.167
It's the three-year anniversary
coming up, you and Joe Jonas.

00:00:22.167 --> 00:00:24.000
-Three year marriage
anniversary.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:25.534
-Wow.
-I think it's leather.

00:00:25.534 --> 00:00:27.000
-Three is leather?

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.434
-I think so, yeah.
-Yeah. Interesting.

00:00:29.434 --> 00:00:30.701
Do you have any thoughts?
-Not a clue.

00:00:30.701 --> 00:00:32.734
-Pair of shoes?

00:00:32.734 --> 00:00:35.100
-Yeah, maybe a pair of shoes.
A book.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.400
-A book.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:38.000
When did you realize, you go,

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.834
"Oh, I think I'm going
to marry Joe Jonas"?

00:00:41.834 --> 00:00:44.501
-I mean, the first night
I met him, I remember --

00:00:44.501 --> 00:00:45.834
like, he left my apartment,

00:00:45.834 --> 00:00:47.434
and it may have been
the alcohol,

00:00:47.434 --> 00:00:49.033
but, like, he left.

00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:51.367
-What was the apartment?
He just came over for a date.

00:00:51.367 --> 00:00:53.267
-He didn't come over.
No, I'm not that forward.

00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:56.767
We went out and we hung out
at a bar with, like,

00:00:56.767 --> 00:00:58.601
all my friends
and all his friends,

00:00:58.601 --> 00:01:00.300
and then they all came back
to my apartment

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:01.467
and we had drinks after.

00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:02.968
-Yeah.

00:01:02.968 --> 00:01:06.067
-And I remember him leaving,
and I just, like, weeped.

00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:07.467
I wept to my brother.

00:01:07.467 --> 00:01:10.934
I was like, "I love
this man so much!"

00:01:10.934 --> 00:01:11.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.968 --> 00:01:13.601
And I knew. And that was it.

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:15.200
-So you knew? Yeah.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:18.634
We know Joe Jonas
as a smooth guy.

00:01:18.634 --> 00:01:21.100
You know,
he's got a lot of game.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:22.767
But then you just told me
something backstage.

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:23.901
You had to call him out on it.

00:01:23.901 --> 00:01:25.934
What did he say to you?

00:01:25.934 --> 00:01:29.701
-So on this first date,
he was like, you know,

00:01:29.701 --> 00:01:31.200
"Do you ever get told --"

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:33.501
He was like,
leading me into this, okay?

00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:36.968
He goes like, "Oh, do you ever
get told you look like,

00:01:36.968 --> 00:01:38.767
you know, a young celebrity?"

00:01:38.767 --> 00:01:42.400
And I was like, "Oh, yeah,
sometimes, but why did you ask?"

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:45.801
And he goes, "Well, I get young
George Clooney all the time."

00:01:45.801 --> 00:01:48.133
And I was like, "No, you don't."

00:01:48.133 --> 00:01:49.567
-[ Laughing ]

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:51.067
-That's such a funny move.

00:01:51.067 --> 00:01:52.767
-No, you don't.

00:01:52.767 --> 00:01:54.501
-That's hilarious,
that he would do that.

00:01:54.501 --> 00:01:55.801
-I know.

00:01:55.801 --> 00:01:58.000
And then I told him,
"Well, I got young Boy George

00:01:58.000 --> 00:02:00.601
all the time, so it's like --

00:02:00.601 --> 00:02:02.334
the Georges combined."

00:02:02.334 --> 00:02:05.234
-Young Boy George Clooney.
Yeah, of course.

00:02:05.234 --> 00:02:06.934
-That's our daughter's name,
actually.

00:02:06.934 --> 00:02:08.234
-Exactly.

00:02:08.234 --> 00:02:09.567
You guys looked great
at the Met Gala the other night.

00:02:09.567 --> 00:02:10.667
Of course you did.

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:11.701
Look, this is
a good-looking couple.

00:02:11.701 --> 00:02:12.868
Oh, my gosh.

00:02:12.868 --> 00:02:13.868
[ Applause ]

00:02:13.868 --> 00:02:16.267
Beautiful. Stunning.

00:02:16.267 --> 00:02:18.634
You've been to
the Met Gala before.

00:02:18.634 --> 00:02:19.801
Do you get starstruck anymore?

00:02:19.801 --> 00:02:22.434
Is there any celebrities
you're like, "Ooh, wow"?

00:02:22.434 --> 00:02:25.234
-I mean, I'm really bad
around celebrities.

00:02:25.234 --> 00:02:29.100
Like, I just can't --
I can't quite fathom

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:31.067
the I'm actually invited
to these things

00:02:31.067 --> 00:02:33.400
and I'm not like
a competition winner, you know?

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:37.901
So I mean, every celebrity
I come into contact with,

00:02:37.901 --> 00:02:40.067
I act up or
say something stupid.

00:02:40.067 --> 00:02:43.601
And recently, it's been if
a celebrity interacts with me,

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:46.367
I immediately just
shut them down and I'm like,

00:02:46.367 --> 00:02:47.501
"I don't want anything
to do with you."

00:02:47.501 --> 00:02:51.000
And I secretly I'm like,
"Oh, my God."

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.334
-"I love you!" "Hey, 'sup."
-I love you so much!

00:02:52.334 --> 00:02:55.501
-Yeah, but I've gone too far
the other way before,

00:02:55.501 --> 00:02:56.901
so I guess I've --

00:02:56.901 --> 00:02:58.300
-What's a recent example?

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:01.334
-So Kendall Jenner was
at the --

00:03:01.334 --> 00:03:03.601
Have you ever heard of her?
She's very --

00:03:03.601 --> 00:03:04.901
-We've heard of her, yeah.
-She's a niche.

00:03:04.901 --> 00:03:07.300
-Yes.
-She was at the Met.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:10.167
And I love the Kardashians,

00:03:10.167 --> 00:03:13.300
but I think she's
so gorgeous in real life.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:15.267
And I was so, like,
struck by her beauty,

00:03:15.267 --> 00:03:17.300
and she, like, invited me to --

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:19.367
they were having,
like, this afterparty,

00:03:19.367 --> 00:03:21.501
this low-key afterparty.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:23.367
And she went, like,
"Do you want to come?"

00:03:23.367 --> 00:03:25.200
And I just went, "No."

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:26.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:28.033
"No. No, I don't."

00:03:28.033 --> 00:03:31.067
And I'm like, why?
Why do I do this to myself?

00:03:31.067 --> 00:03:33.067
"I would love to come!"
You're like, "Nah.

00:03:33.067 --> 00:03:34.300
No, I'm good. Nah, later."

00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:36.300
-And then I just sat in bed
and ate pasta,

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.434
and I was like, "Could be
somewhere else right now."

00:03:38.434 --> 00:03:40.000
-That sounds pretty good,
by the way,

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:41.300
sitting in bed and eating pasta.

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.367
-You know, it wasn't bad.
-Yeah, it wasn't bad. Yeah.

00:03:43.367 --> 00:03:46.467
I want to talk about
your new show, "The Staircase."

00:03:46.467 --> 00:03:49.934
Congrats on this.
I know the documentary.

00:03:49.934 --> 00:03:51.334
I've seen it.
-Yes.

00:03:51.334 --> 00:03:52.868
I mean, when did you
get into it?

00:03:52.868 --> 00:03:54.234
When did you hear about it?

00:03:54.234 --> 00:03:57.267
-I think I got into it
when everyone else kind of did.

00:03:57.267 --> 00:04:00.968
I think it was like 2020,
it came out on Netflix

00:04:00.968 --> 00:04:03.968
and everyone became, like,
completely obsessed with it.

00:04:03.968 --> 00:04:06.067
-It's insane.
-It's insane.

00:04:06.067 --> 00:04:09.167
And so about six months later,

00:04:09.167 --> 00:04:11.200
I found out they were making
an HBO show about it.

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:13.167
And I was like,
I mean, sign me up.

00:04:13.167 --> 00:04:15.968
I kind of remember
what happened, but I also don't.

00:04:15.968 --> 00:04:19.901
So there's the husband --
-So, yeah.

00:04:19.901 --> 00:04:21.667
So this woman,
Kathleen Peterson --

00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:24.133
This is a true story.
-Yes.

00:04:24.133 --> 00:04:29.400
-She either fell or was pushed
by someone down the stairs.

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.467
Unfortunately, she passed away.

00:04:31.467 --> 00:04:34.667
And the whole documentary
is following

00:04:34.667 --> 00:04:38.567
the trial of her husband,
Michael Peterson,

00:04:38.567 --> 00:04:42.334
who they believed
pushed her down the stairs.

00:04:42.334 --> 00:04:45.367
-Yeah.
-And so this show is about that.

00:04:45.367 --> 00:04:50.968
But it's not another
telling of the same thing.

00:04:50.968 --> 00:04:54.100
It actually is about the making
of the documentary

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:55.767
on top of the case
that's going on,

00:04:55.767 --> 00:04:56.834
because there's

00:04:56.834 --> 00:04:58.567
layers and layers
and layers of corruption.

00:04:58.567 --> 00:05:00.167
-Did your opinion change

00:05:00.167 --> 00:05:03.067
while you were filming this,
of what happened?

00:05:03.067 --> 00:05:05.901
-I'm so done talking
about what happened.

00:05:05.901 --> 00:05:07.834
I mean, we were on set
and it was just like --

00:05:07.834 --> 00:05:08.968
-I had theories.
My wife had theories.

00:05:08.968 --> 00:05:10.601
-Everyone have theories.

00:05:10.601 --> 00:05:13.267
And I was theorizing
for so long,

00:05:13.267 --> 00:05:16.167
and then by this point,
I'm like, I just --

00:05:16.167 --> 00:05:17.667
-Yeah.
-I'm over it.

00:05:17.667 --> 00:05:20.067
-Exactly. Yeah.
-I'm over it.

00:05:20.067 --> 00:05:22.000
-It's fascinating.
Fascinating story.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:24.400
-Fascinating.
-And your great great cast,

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:26.267
Colin Firth,
our buddy Toni Collette.

00:05:26.267 --> 00:05:28.000
-Amazing.
-I mean, so many.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:30.868
Rosemarie DeWitt,
Dane DeHaan, Juliette Binoche.

00:05:30.868 --> 00:05:34.334
Michael Stuhlbarg.
I mean, the list goes on.

00:05:34.334 --> 00:05:35.701
-I was asking you if, you know,

00:05:35.701 --> 00:05:37.934
because it gets intense talking
about this type of stuff.

00:05:37.934 --> 00:05:39.334
Do you ever
make it loose on set?

00:05:39.334 --> 00:05:40.367
What was the fun things?

00:05:40.367 --> 00:05:43.300
And you said
that you created a game.

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:44.767
It's called "Yea or Nay."

00:05:44.767 --> 00:05:46.901
-It's called "Yea or Nay."
-That's correct.

00:05:46.901 --> 00:05:48.834
It was invented --

00:05:48.834 --> 00:05:49.868
Well, I don't know
if it was invented,

00:05:49.868 --> 00:05:51.868
but was brought to me
by Odessa Young,

00:05:51.868 --> 00:05:53.167
who plays my sister
on the show.

00:05:53.167 --> 00:05:54.901
-Wait, someone actually --

00:05:54.901 --> 00:05:56.167
I thought
you invented this game.

00:05:56.167 --> 00:05:57.601
-I didn't invent this game.

00:05:57.601 --> 00:05:59.033
-This is a real game.
-I can't take credit for this.

00:05:59.033 --> 00:06:00.334
This is real game.

00:06:00.334 --> 00:06:01.901
-Can you explain to everyone
what this game is?

00:06:01.901 --> 00:06:05.934
-It's very basic, but basically,
it's a great time waster.

00:06:05.934 --> 00:06:13.234
So one person is the subject and
everyone else secretly decides,

00:06:13.234 --> 00:06:15.968
"This is the end position that
we want this person

00:06:15.968 --> 00:06:17.267
to end up in."

00:06:17.267 --> 00:06:20.100
Okay, so you choose
a physical position for them.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:21.634
It could be like this.

00:06:21.634 --> 00:06:23.234
It could be like,
climbing on the wall.

00:06:23.234 --> 00:06:24.701
It could be anything.

00:06:24.701 --> 00:06:26.067
-You all decide that
that's the position.

00:06:26.067 --> 00:06:27.300
-And you all decide.

00:06:27.300 --> 00:06:29.701
And then you just kind of
let the subject go

00:06:29.701 --> 00:06:33.000
and move around the space,
move their body.

00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:34.767
And you say, yea
if they're getting warmer

00:06:34.767 --> 00:06:37.567
to the pose,
or nay if they're not.

00:06:37.567 --> 00:06:39.200
And I think we should play it.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:40.434
-We should play this?
-I think we should play it.

00:06:40.434 --> 00:06:41.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:41.901 --> 00:06:43.734
-I love this.

00:06:43.734 --> 00:06:45.267
I love any game.

00:06:45.267 --> 00:06:46.801
I love anyone bringing a game.
-Are you down?

00:06:46.801 --> 00:06:50.100
-I'm down. How do we do it?
-Get yourself up.

00:06:50.100 --> 00:06:52.968
-Okay.
-I will...

00:06:52.968 --> 00:06:55.234
You know, conveniently,
there's a whiteboard here.

00:06:55.234 --> 00:06:56.834
I don't know how that got there.

00:06:56.834 --> 00:06:59.133
I will write down the position

00:06:59.133 --> 00:07:01.467
that I want you to end up in.

00:07:01.467 --> 00:07:02.501
-Okay. I'm not looking.

00:07:02.501 --> 00:07:04.200
-I'll show you guys,
the audience.

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:06.267
-So the audience is in
on the position?

00:07:06.267 --> 00:07:08.234
-Yes.
-This is "Yea or Nay."

00:07:08.234 --> 00:07:11.667
-And then we will
say yea or nay,

00:07:11.667 --> 00:07:13.634
depending on if
you're getting closer or not.

00:07:13.634 --> 00:07:14.868
-Okay, "Yea or Nay."

00:07:14.868 --> 00:07:16.701
And this is a real game
that someone made up.

00:07:16.701 --> 00:07:17.767
[ Laughter ]

00:07:17.767 --> 00:07:19.634
-Okay, can we see?

00:07:19.634 --> 00:07:21.667
-You're showing?
I'm not looking.

00:07:21.667 --> 00:07:22.767
-Yeah?

00:07:22.767 --> 00:07:24.100
[ Applause ]

00:07:24.100 --> 00:07:26.100
-Our audience likes it.

00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:27.901
Alright. Is it away, Sophie?

00:07:27.901 --> 00:07:29.100
-It's away.
-It is away.

00:07:29.100 --> 00:07:30.334
It's gone.
-Okay. Alright.

00:07:30.334 --> 00:07:32.033
So now are we currently
playing "Yea or Nay"?

00:07:32.033 --> 00:07:33.367
-We're currently playing.

00:07:33.367 --> 00:07:34.534
-[ Laughing ]

00:07:34.534 --> 00:07:35.601
-Move about the space.

00:07:35.601 --> 00:07:38.300
I'm moving about the space.
Okay.

00:07:38.300 --> 00:07:39.868
-All: Nay.

00:07:42.834 --> 00:07:45.567
Nay.

00:07:45.567 --> 00:07:47.934
Yea.

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:50.934
[ Laughing ]

00:07:50.934 --> 00:07:53.267
Yea.

00:07:53.334 --> 00:07:54.901
Nay.

00:07:54.901 --> 00:07:56.767
Yea!

00:07:56.834 --> 00:07:58.167
Yea! Yea.

00:07:58.234 --> 00:08:03.267
Yea!

00:08:03.334 --> 00:08:04.400
Yea.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:06.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
-You did it!

00:08:06.434 --> 00:08:08.300
[ Bell dings ]

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:11.367
-Wow, I'm an expert!

00:08:11.367 --> 00:08:13.534
At "Yea or Nay," I'm an expert!
-I can't believe you got it!

00:08:13.534 --> 00:08:14.834
-Is that what it was?

00:08:14.834 --> 00:08:15.934
-Yes, that was it!

00:08:15.934 --> 00:08:17.234
All fours on desk.

00:08:17.234 --> 00:08:18.734
-Oh, my gosh.

00:08:18.734 --> 00:08:20.367
-There it is.
-All fours on desk.

00:08:20.367 --> 00:08:21.734
That's what I'm talking about!

00:08:21.734 --> 00:08:22.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:22.801 --> 00:08:24.467
"Yea or Nay."
You are the most fun.

00:08:24.467 --> 00:08:26.868
I want to show everyone
a clip.

00:08:26.868 --> 00:08:28.501
Here's Sophie Turner
in "The Staircase."

00:08:28.501 --> 00:08:30.100
Take a look at this.

00:08:30.100 --> 00:08:31.634
-Hey, Dad.

00:08:31.634 --> 00:08:34.801
-You guys unwrap presents yet?
-No, not yet.

00:08:34.801 --> 00:08:36.367
-They're not going
to do it themselves.

00:08:36.367 --> 00:08:37.767
-I know. It's just --

00:08:37.767 --> 00:08:39.701
It's not the same without you.

00:08:39.701 --> 00:08:42.367
-Honey, nothing
feels right about this.

00:08:45.100 --> 00:08:46.567
-The D.A. keeps calling.

00:08:46.567 --> 00:08:49.234
-Well, you just
keep ignoring them.

00:08:49.234 --> 00:08:53.567
So, have you spoken
to Candace Zamperini?

00:08:53.567 --> 00:08:55.133
I haven't gotten through.

00:08:55.133 --> 00:08:56.467
-Uh, no.

00:08:56.467 --> 00:08:58.968
What, really? Nothing?

00:08:58.968 --> 00:09:03.701
-No.

00:09:03.701 --> 00:09:08.300
-Look, just make sure
everyone sticks together.

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:09.834
I miss you.

00:09:09.834 --> 00:09:12.434
-I miss you, too. We all do.

00:09:12.434 --> 00:09:14.300
-I'll see you soon, alright?

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:16.033
-Okay.
-I love you.

00:09:16.033 --> 00:09:17.100
-I love you.

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:19.100
-Sophie Turner, everybody!

00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:20.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:20.400 --> 00:09:22.601
The first three episodes
of "The Staircase"

00:09:22.601 --> 00:09:24.968
are streaming now
on HBO Max.

